# ─── Syntax Quick Reference ───────────────────────────────────────────────────
# <trigger>:<command1> ; <command2>        →  chain multiple with ;
# >>Title|Subtitle|Seconds                 →  overlay text (on-screen)
# /command                                 →  Minecraft vanilla (datapack)
# !command                                 →  RCON (direct to server)
# $name                                    →  hook script (Python)
# &command                                 →  shell command (PC, e.g. webhook)
# @slot>>Title                             →  overlay in named slot
# x<number>                                →  multiplier (run command N times)
# {user}                                   →  placeholder: viewer name
# {comment}                                →  placeholder: comment text (comment trigger only)
# ## <trigger>:...                         →  disabled (kept as template)
# Gift ID format:  <position><id>          →  e.g. 1<id> = slot 1, 8<id> = slot 8
# All gift IDs and names: defaults/gifts.json
# ─── Event Examples ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

# 1. Follow: golden apple + overlay (; chains both)
follow:/give @a minecraft:golden_apple 7 ; >>New Follower!|{user} is now following!|5

# 2. Likes (every 100): creeper spawn with x3 multiplier
likes:/execute at @a run summon minecraft:creeper ~ ~ ~ x3

# 3. Like mega (default: 100k): clear inventory + kill all
like_2:/clear @a * ; /kill @a

# 4. Comment: display chat message in overlay ({comment} works here only)
comment:>>{user} wrote:|{comment}

# 5. Share: fireworks for everyone (simple /give)
share:/give @a minecraft:firework_rocket 3

# ─── Gift Examples ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

# 6. Rosa (ID 913): summon 3 evokers (multiplier x3 on the command)
8913:/execute at @a run summon minecraft:evoker ~ ~ ~ x3

# 7. Mamma Mia (ID 16111): diamonds + overlay (chained)
16111:/give @a minecraft:diamond ; >>Mamma Mia!|{user} sent Mamma Mia!|4

# 8. Tom the Tomato (ID 16379): random trigger ($random)
16379:$random

# ─── Advanced Examples ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

# 9. Quoted trigger name (needed when the name contains spaces)
'Tom the Tomato':/give @a minecraft:potato 1

# 10. Shell command: Discord webhook on follow (PC-side)
#follow:&curl -X POST -H "Content-Type: application/json" -d "{\"content\":\"{user} just followed!\"}" https://discord.com/api/webhooks/YOUR_WEBHOOK

# 11. Disabled with ## – kept as template, won't fire
# Note: like_2 is already used above, so this entry would be ignored if enabled. Keep it disabled as a template.
##like_2:/kill @a

# 12. Disabled gift with TNT parameters (requires TNT plugin)
##5655:!tnt 2 0.1 2 Notch